 "notes": "The generic opponent assembler's library (NP_04 s9): pieces tagged Style x House-dialect x tier, and the rules that build a non-named opponent's pattern from them in the shape the sim executes (meta, strings, select, interrupt, punish; no bait, phases, desperation or idle lines - generics are patterns, not characters). 36 string pieces (9 per Style: three tiers of an opener and two others, tier 3's third the Style's SPECIAL), 12 punish hooks (3 per Style, one per tier; {lead} / {second} / {third} name the assembled strings), 15 tell dialects (a channel and motifs by class: the 13 named Houses of NP_07 s8 that have one, the school's, and the gym's for a no-name). The rules: strings by tier (2 at tier 1, 3 above), one PUNISH, one tell channel per dialect, SELECT weights from the Style presets, the interrupt block by tier, tells shifted into the tier's band (Loud / Standard / Subtle, NP_04 s3) and floored by class (NP_04 s1). Named-boss strings never appear: no piece shares a label or an action sequence with any of the 24 (a smoke gate holds it). The difficulty knob = piece tier + tell tier + the stat block by tier (a card's stats override). Every value here is a first draft; the launch library's 60 pieces are the content lane's.",
